        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Events: 55th Academy Awards\n- Places: Dorothy Chandler Pavilion, Los Angeles Music Center, Los Angeles, London, England\n- Works: A Shocking Accident\n- People: Olly Blackburn\n- Awards: Academy Award for Best Live Action Short, Best Short Subject\n\nFacts:\n- The 55th Academy Awards were presented on April 11, 1983, at the Dorothy Chandler Pavilion in Los Angeles.\n- The Dorothy Chandler Pavilion is one of the halls in the Los Angeles Music Center, which is one of the three largest performing arts centers in the United States.\n- A Shocking Accident is a 1982 short comedy film.\n- In 1983, A Shocking Accident won an Academy Award at the 55th Academy Awards for Best Live Action Short.\n- Olly Blackburn was born in London, England.\n- Olly Blackburn had an acting role in A Shocking Accident.",
